rulings: ["[{'date': '2011-01-01', 'text': 'It must be clear to all players which token has deathtouch and which token has lifelink.'}, {'date': '2011-01-01', 'text': 'The two creature tokens enter the battlefield at the same time.'}]", "[{'date': '2015-02-25', 'text': 'Each of the creature cards can have mana value 3 or less. It’s not the total mana value of the two cards.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-06-23\', \'text\': "If you control four or more lands, the basic land doesn\'t enter the battlefield untapped; it enters tapped and then you untap it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-06-23\', \'text\': \'The land that you put onto the battlefield will be counted when determining whether you control four or more lands, but Fabled Passage will not.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won\'t return to the battlefield."}, {\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "If you gain control of a creature “until end of turn,” you control it during that turn\'s end step."}, {\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "Once the exiled creature returns, it\'s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled creature will be put into their owners\' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled creature will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creature will cease to exist."}, {\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "When an effect returns the exiled card “under your control,” you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Conjurer\'s Closet effect are exiled."}]']
